=You write the questions real buyers type into ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Google's AI Mode before they choose a provider. These questions are asked every day and every week to measure whether the business below is recommended or cited by AI assistants, so they must be realistic, varied and stable.

BUSINESS
Name: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.business_name }} · Website: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.domain }} · Type: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.business_type || 'see the topics' }}
Market: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.country || 'not given' }}{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.city ? ' (' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.city + ')' : '' }} · Write the questions in {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.language || 'English' }}
Buyer role asking: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.persona ? $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.persona + ' — write every question as this person would type it (their concerns, their vocabulary, their decision)' : 'choose a realistic buyer role per question (e.g. owner, finance, IT, operations) and give it in "persona"' }}
Topics it wants to be found for: {{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.topics || []).join(' · ') || 'infer from the website name' }}
{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.focus_topics || []).length ? 'THESE QUESTIONS ARE ABOUT THESE TOPICS ONLY, this many for each: ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.focus_topics.map(t => t.label + ' (' + t.count + ')').join(' · ') + '. Every question is about one of them or one of its sub-topics (' + ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.topics || []).join(' · ') + '), and its cluster is that topic, written exactly as above.\n' : '' }}{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.clusters || []).length ? 'Topic clusters already used by the panel (reuse these names for questions on the same service; add a new cluster only for a service none of them covers): ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.clusters.join(' · ') + '\n' : '' }}
{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.site_text ? 'WEBSITE TEXT (the homepage, to understand what the business sells):\n' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.site_text + '\n' : '' }}{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.market_questions || []).length ? 'REAL QUESTIONS PEOPLE ASK AI ABOUT THESE TOPICS (from a database of AI answers, with monthly AI search volume; prefer these, adapted to buyer wording, when they fit the business):\n- ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.market_questions.join('\n- ') + '\n' : '' }}{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.search_questions || []).length ? 'SEARCHES THE WEBSITE ALREADY APPEARS FOR ON GOOGLE (long or question-shaped; good signals of what buyers ask):\n- ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.search_questions.join('\n- ') + '\n' : '' }}{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.paa_questions || []).length ? 'QUESTIONS GOOGLE SHOWS IN "PEOPLE ALSO ASK" FOR THESE TOPICS (real questions; adapt them to the buyer role):\n- ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.paa_questions.join('\n- ') + '\n' : '' }}{{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.competitor_offers || []).length ? 'WHAT COMPETITORS\' HOMEPAGES SAY THEY SELL (topic ideas only — never put a competitor\'s name in a question):\n- ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.competitor_offers.join('\n- ') + '\n' : '' }}Questions already tracked (do not repeat or rephrase them): {{ ($('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.existing || []).join(' | ') || 'none' }}

Write exactly {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.count }} new questions. Spread them over the buyer journey and the topics, most valuable first:
- recommend: "Which companies / who are the best … in <market>?" — the questions where AI lists providers (about 40% of the questions)
- choose: how to choose, what to look for, red flags
- cost: price, cost, fees, budget
- compare: X vs Y, alternatives, which option is better for a given situation
- problem: the problem the buyer wants solved, in their words (deadline, regulation, failure, migration)
{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.shopping ? '- shopping: what a shopper types before buying one of the products this business sells ("best <product> for <use> under <price>", "where to buy <product> in <market>"), the questions where AI shows product cards (about 20% of the questions; this business sells products: ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.shopping_why + ')\n' : '' }}{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.has_brand_prompt ? '' : '- brand: exactly one question asking what ' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.business_name + ' (' + $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.domain + ') is and offers — this checks whether AI knows the brand' }}

For each question give:
- kind: recommend | choose | cost | compare | problem | brand{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.shopping ? ' | shopping' : '' }}
- stage: awareness (learning about the problem) | consideration (comparing options) | decision (choosing a provider, price, "best", "near me") | brand{{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.shopping ? ' | shopping (a shopper about to buy a product)' : '' }}
- cluster: the topic group in 1-4 words (questions about the same service share one cluster name)
- keyword: a short Google search phrase (2-6 words) for the same intent
- origin: market (adapted from the real AI questions above) | search (from the Google searches above) | paa (from "People also ask") | competitor (from what competitors sell) | writer (your own)
- persona: the buyer role asking ({{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.persona || 'your choice, 1-3 words' }})

Rules: {{ $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.place_rule ? $('Any Prompt Jobs?').item.json.place_rule + ' ' : '' }}plain buyer language, 8-22 words, the market named where the buyer would name it, no company or product names at all (not even in a comparison: compare the kinds of solution, e.g. "cloud ERP vs on-premise ERP", never two vendors; a question naming another vendor is refused and never asked), never the business name except in the single brand question, no government service (a ministry's own portal, a visa, an ID card), and every question about something this business sells. Two questions that ask the same thing in other words count as one: make each one different.

Return ONLY JSON: {"prompts": [{"prompt": "", "kind": "", "stage": "", "cluster": "", "keyword": "", "origin": "", "persona": ""}]}

